(text "IN100 insect tag v5: 8 mm round tag, wire antenna, cut-off programming tab" (at 25.4 167.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 53423058-8439-4629-ac6a-257a5a15c497))
(text "- U1 IN100 QFN18 (JLC C6062024). CHIP_EN, VDDQ and VCC tied together; unused GPIOs, switches and RTC pins left open." (at 25.4 170.434 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 37f7f355-c015-4c7c-af22-52e6c87a0fb6))
(text "- Supply 3.3 V on the tab pads while burning the OTP; never with the cell fitted." (at 25.4 173.228 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 1eb13091-63b0-4592-a50c-ac2875006bdc))
(text "- Y1 26 MHz 1612, 7 pF load: the IN100's on-chip load capacitance replaces external caps." (at 25.4 176.022 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid a7e67e2d-bc3c-4acf-bc1d-002ef8d2ab97))
(text "- C1 100 nF at VCC. C2 100 uF 0805: the 337 cell (~80 ohm) cannot supply 9-14 mA TX bursts alone." (at 25.4 178.816 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 5c80ad0a-def4-45c5-a2af-105ea5d27a45))
(text "- AE1: ~30 mm enamelled wire in a plated hole, fed straight from RF_TX (trim to tune)." (at 25.4 181.61 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid e2363ca1-3a4f-4e87-b447-032b719b9dff))
(text "- BT1: 337 / SR416SW cell under the tag: - cap silver-epoxied to the underside pad, + wire to the top rim pad." (at 25.4 184.404 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 2d9cc943-2b43-4cae-8b43-3396ce25fb66))
(text "- J1: 2 x 2 plated pads on the tab (R T / + G); cut the neck after programming." (at 25.4 187.198 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 5ae27027-63be-4c51-9157-75e86f3ade20))
(text "Derived from the IN100 datasheet reference design and SparkFun's NanoBeacon Lite board (CC BY-SA 4.0)." (at 25.4 189.992 0) (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 4765bd9d-a8f2-4b12-a366-a9984a60193c))
